pawed through every darn thing we owned, every piece of clothing, our toiletries, rifling
through the pages of our books, probing into each suitcase – everything. They didn’t
find anything they were interested in, just like I had told them. When they finished with
the luggage, leaving all of our stuff strewn across the bed in piles and some on the floor,
they turned their attention to where the dog was sitting. I saw them squat down and
poke around with something, maybe a pencil. The guy pulled a panel off the wall and
took out a small plastic bag. I had no idea what they found.
TIM: Okay, what did the Customs agents say or do?
